WEBVTT

00:00:01.550 --> 00:00:12.353
<v Safi>I see two routes. One leads onto high rock ledges. The other goes under the meadow. Which animal uses which route?

00:00:15.653 --> 00:00:20.942
<v Nuri>Start at the ledge. Watch how a mountain goat places its foot on uneven rock.

00:00:24.242 --> 00:00:30.646
<v Safi>I thought the hoof was a single piece. Up close I can see two parts at the tip.

00:00:31.196 --> 00:00:38.085
<v Nuri>Look from underneath. The two toes can spread, and their soft inner pads help grip the rock.

00:00:41.385 --> 00:00:48.266
<v Safi>Here is a real mountain goat. I can see its thick white coat and its horns.

00:00:51.566 --> 00:01:00.535
<v Nuri>Back to the meadow by the rocks. Can you spot the brown fur at the burrow? Watch what the animal eats.

00:01:03.835 --> 00:01:11.518
<v Safi>The marmot is eating grass. When snow covers this meadow in winter, what will it eat?

00:01:12.067 --> 00:01:19.356
<v Nuri>While food is plentiful, marmots eat plants and store energy in their bodies as fat.

00:01:22.657 --> 00:01:29.540
<v Safi>The same meadow has turned white. There’s no marmot on the rock. Is it underground?

00:01:30.089 --> 00:01:40.018
<v Nuri>Yes. It hibernates in its underground burrow. Its heart slows, its body uses less energy, and it lives on stored fat.

00:01:43.318 --> 00:01:51.238
<v Safi>Here is a real yellow-bellied marmot. Compare its coat with the mountain goat we saw earlier.

00:01:54.538 --> 00:02:01.667
<v Nuri>If the clues are two toes and soft pads, which route would you choose?

00:02:04.767 --> 00:02:12.049
<v Safi>The goat’s rocky ledge! The burrow beneath the meadow is where the marmot hibernates.

00:02:15.349 --> 00:02:23.738
<v Safi>We found our answers by watching from a distance. Thank Allah for creating both animals and enabling them to live on the mountain.
